## 12. Verdict

  FAIL, round 1. One blocking finding (F-1): inventory B — behaviour 4's whole
  reason for existing — scans a narrower shape than the spec of record specifies,
  the narrowing was never reported through the amendment channel the builder
  otherwise used correctly twice, the brief's own censor-only acceptance check (e)
  does not bite, and red 04's mF passes only because the harness named its probe
  parameter to fit the filter.

  Everything else in this opus is sound and should be kept as it stands: four
  gates green, the contract table covers what it promises, the collision-sentinel
  recipe does real work at all nine rows, inventory A is alias- and reformat-proof
  and bites on both required cases, the harness's kills-AND and restore discipline
  are faithful to the brief, the brief amendment is the standard I would want, and
  the red re-record is honest correction rather than backfilling.

  Fix scope for round 2 is F-1 alone, plus F-2 and F-3 if the architect wants them
  folded in; F-4 is a retro item.
